## Why This Is Asked

Tests a practical, beginner-friendly ML pipeline for churn with real-world constraints: leakage prevention, encoding choices, and model comparisons that balance performance and interpretability.

## Key Concepts

- Data leakage prevention via time-based or grouped splits
- Handling class imbalance in binary targets
- Baseline vs tree-based models and interpretability
- Evaluation metrics: AUROC andPR-AUC, plus feature importance tools like SHAP

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo baseline pipeline (illustrative only)
function trainBaseline(data){
  const X = oneHotEncode(data.features);
  const {train, test} = timeSplit(X, data.labels);
  const model = trainLR(train.features, train.labels, {C:1.0});
  const preds = model.predict(test.features);
  return evaluate(test.labels, preds);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt this for a much larger dataset?
- What monitoring would you set up to detect data drift over time?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical on-device ML design, multilingual handling, and privacy-preserving model updates with realistic latency targets.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML, model distillation, language gating
- Local retrieval for context, approximate nearest neighbor search
- DP-SGD, secure aggregation, rollout plans, drift detection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo latency measurement snippet
async function measureLatency(model, input){
  const t0 = performance.now();
  await model.predict(input);
  const t1 = performance.now();
  return t1 - t0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate multilingual latency across devices?
- How would you handle data drift in languages with scarce data?

Why This Is Asked
- Tests ability to design robust, low-latency hybrid ML systems under distribution shift.
- Probes gating, calibration, drift handling, and online experimentation.

Key Concepts
- Hybrid models, gating mechanisms, calibration, drift detection, online A/B testing, latency budgets.

Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for gating logic
function route(transaction, gateModel, fastDetector, autoencoder) {
  const uncertainty = gateModel.predict(transaction);
  if (uncertainty > THRESHOLD) return autoencoder.detect(transaction);
  return fastDetector.detect(transaction);
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor drift windows and decide retraining cadence?
- How would you securely log data for online experimentation and ensure latency budgets are met?

## Why This Is Asked

This tests practical transfer learning on small data, calibration awareness, and a simple data-collection loop.

## Key Concepts

- Transfer learning with lightweight nets
- Data augmentation for small datasets
- Probability calibration (temperature scaling)
- Active/incremental labeling
- Evaluation: accuracy and calibration metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: load pretrained MobileNetV2, replace head, train on 2k images
const model = loadPretrained('MobileNetV2');
model.detachHead();
model.addHead(5);
model.freezeLayers(['conv1','conv2']);
model.compile({lr: 1e-4, loss: 'categoricalCrossentropy', optimizer:'adam'});
model.fit(dataset, {epochs: 5, augment: true});
```

